      situation: `${SETTING} To save time, a colleague asked an [[c|LLM]] to read the methods section of the household study and pull out every parameter the city's [[b|SEIR model]] needs. The table came back in seconds and looks complete.`,
      question: "Which extracted parameters can go into the model as they are, which are wrong, and how do you set up LLM extraction so errors like these get caught?",
