    takeaways: ["An LLM predicts number [[c|tokens]]; plausible is not correct, and it may fill rows the source never reported.", "Rates are 1/mean duration: [[w|copying a duration into a rate field]] breaks the model.", "Early case data identifies the growth rate r; separating R0 from the durations needs independent evidence ([[w|identifiability]]).", "Use [[t|structured outputs]] with quoted spans and mechanical checks; do conversions in tested code."],
