      situation: `${SETTING} The cell keeps a library of past outbreaks in a [[t|vector database]]. Each record stores the first six weeks of reported cases as a vector, plus metadata. The director asks: "Have we seen an epidemic like this before, and what happened next?"`,
      question: "Which past outbreaks are genuinely comparable to Port Calder, and how much should their outcomes shape our priors?",
      objectives: ["Explain what a curve [[c|embedding]] captures and what it ignores", "Choose between [[c|cosine similarity]] and [[c|Euclidean distance]] for shape versus size", "Combine similarity with [[c|metadata filters]]", "Use analogues as [[w|priors, not predictions]]"],
      evidence: VDB_EVIDENCE,
