    takeaways: ["MCP: **host** (app + LLM + policy), **client** (one per server), **server** (capabilities).", "JSON-RPC 2.0 flow: `initialize` → `notifications/initialized` → `tools/list` → `tools/call`.", "[[t|Tools]] are model-controlled, [[t|resources]] are readable data, [[t|prompts]] are templates; transports are stdio or Streamable HTTP.", "[[c|Least privilege]], human approval for side effects, OAuth-based auth for HTTP, and [[w|tool output is data, not instructions]]."],
    summary: "MCP roles (host, client, server); JSON-RPC 2.0 requests/responses/notifications; initialize, notifications/initialized, tools/list with JSON Schema, tools/call; tools vs resources (resources/list, resources/read) vs prompts (prompts/list, prompts/get); stdio vs Streamable HTTP; least privilege and human approval; tool annotations (readOnlyHint, destructiveHint) are untrusted hints; OAuth 2.1-based authorization for HTTP; prompt injection via tool results; audit trail for reproducible forecasts.",
